## 6. Measure parsing separately from Kafka

Before replacing the CSV library, run these benchmarks against representative files:

| Test | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Parse CSV and count records, without JSON/Kafka | Measure CSV-reading throughput |
| Parse CSV and serialize JSON, without Kafka | Measure serialization overhead |
| Full pipeline with 1 worker | Establish end-to-end baseline |
| Full pipeline with 2, 4, then 8 workers | Find useful concurrency |

Record:

- Committed records/second.
- Input bytes/second.
- CPU utilization and GC time.
- Disk throughput and latency.
- Transaction commit latency.
- Queue depth per worker.

Choose the smallest worker count that gives near-maximum measured throughput.

**Do not assume virtual threads will make parsing faster.** They help scale waiting tasks; they do not make CPU-intensive parsing or serialization execute faster. ([docs.oracle.com](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/core/virtual-threads.html))

