## 7. Two correctness warnings

### Do not launch another identical application instance casually

This design assumes one active dispatcher for the directory. Multiple active instances need explicit worker ownership; otherwise, they can compete and repeatedly fence the same transactional producers.

### Migrate existing checkpoints before enabling this layout

If the previous deployment has one checkpoint topic, new worker-specific topics will initially be empty. Starting workers against them would reprocess files.

Stop and fence the old writer, recover its committed state, then redistribute checkpoints using the new filename-to-worker assignment. Preserve event identities and verify the migration before starting ingestion.

---

**My recommendation for your case:** keep the single directory, add **4 bounded, independent file workers**, retain byte-offset checkpoints and transactional batches, and benchmark against 1/2/8 workers. That is the next practical throughput improvement without sacrificing recovery semantics.
